# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [3.6.0] - 2026-09-18

### Added

- Add release drafter workflow. (#174) @jenskeiner
- Add macOS build workflow. (#168) @jenskeiner
- Add more compiler versions to CI and dev container. (#166) @jenskeiner
- Add Dependabot config. (#154) @jenskeiner
- Add dev container. (#153) @jenskeiner
- Add Linux build & test workflow. (#150) @jenskeiner
- Add CodSpeed benchmarks. (#148) @jenskeiner
- Add NFSFT interface for Julia and Python. (#143) @mnolander
- Add kernel `der_laplacian_rbf` (#138) @wagnertheresa
- Add kernels xx_gaussian and absx in fastsum. @FranziskaN

### Changed

- Retry benchmarks up to three times. (#187) @jenskeiner
- Link against libatomic where required for OpenMP atomic operations on floating-point type. (#170) @jenskeiner
- Run benchmarks agnostic to certain parameters only for default values. (#162) @jenskeiner
- Refactor CUnit library detection and usage. (#160) @jenskeiner
- Improve threaded FFTW 3 library detection and usage as well as overall link-time behavior. (#158) @jenskeiner
- Improve direct adjoint NDFT transform performance. (#152) @jenskeiner
- Improve direct NDFT forward transform for d > 1. (#149) @jenskeiner
- Improve efficiency of NDFT forward transform for d = 1. (#142) @jenskeiner
- Allow configure to run on ARM. (#140) @ralfHielscher

### Fixed

- Fix compilation errors with GCC 15 in cunit tests (#165) @michaelquellmalz
- Re-enable Julia interface. (#164) @jenskeiner
- Do not modify LIBS in the detection of CUnit. (#163) @michaelquellmalz
- Fix an issue where makedist would fail because doxygen always builds documentation in srcdir, not builddir. (#161) @jenskeiner
- Prevent autoreconf warning in `nfft_lib_codspeed.m4` (#157) @michaelquellmalz
- Fix build with GCC 15 (#146) @DarthGandalf
- Add missing get functions for odd n to imex.h. @michaelquellmalz

### Chores

- Bump actions/upload-artifact from 4.6.2 to 6.0.0 (#186) @[dependabot[bot]](https://github.com/apps/dependabot)
- Bump actions/checkout from 5 to 6 (#179) @[dependabot[bot]](https://github.com/apps/dependabot)
- Harden workflows. (#184) @jenskeiner
- Bump actions/upload-artifact from 4 to 5 (#177) @[dependabot[bot]](https://github.com/apps/dependabot)
- Remove the softlink the README.md (#159) @michaelquellmalz
- Bump CodSpeedHQ/action from 3 to 4 (#155) @[dependabot[bot]](https://github.com/apps/dependabot)
- Bump actions/checkout from 4 to 5 (#156) @[dependabot[bot]](https://github.com/apps/dependabot)
- Add required software and reference in README. (#129) @michaelquellmalz
- Add Bibtex entry in README. @michaelquellmalz

## [3.5.3] - 2022-04-02

### Added

- Additional node at South Pole in `NFSFT_EQUISPACED`. (#118)
- Matlab interface with single precision. (#115)
- Add function `set_num_threads` in Matlab. (#113)

### Fixed

- Fix in the fastsum Matlab interface that might cause crashes. (#116)
- Update obsolete autoconf macros.

## [3.5.2] - 2020-08-25

### Added

- Add Julia interface for fastsum. (#98)
- Even bandwidth in NFCT and NFST. (#105)
- TravisCI tests on Windows and OSX.

### Changed

- Compute `NFFT_EPSILON` at runtime. (#108)
- In-place FFTW for dimension > 1 (reduce memory consumption). (#110)
- Enable AVX2 in precompiled binaries.

### Fixed

- Build of fastsum fails because `fftw_libs` are not found. (#103)
- Update m4 files for 3.5.2 release. (#109)
- Remove superfluous calls to autoreconf in bootstrap.

## [3.5.1] - 2019-08-09

### Added

- Add Julia interface for NFCT, NFST. (#86)
- FSFT: Spherical Fourier transform with equidistant nodes. (#87)
- Inverse NFFT via frame approach. (#88)

### Fixed

- Improve check if tests are executed in Matlab or Octave. (#90)
- Build with Octave 5.1.0 fails in Windows. (#92)
- FFTW3 linking problem while building. (#95)
- Remove unnecessary dependence on ncurses library. (#96)

## [3.5.0] - 2019-01-28

### Added

- Add NFSOFT Matlab class. (#76)
- Add MEX interface for FPT. (#77)
- Add NFFT Julia interface. (#82)

### Changed

- Extend NFFT Matlab interface to d > 4. (#62)
- Faster NFFT in 4D and 5D. (#64)
- Add support for higher bandwidth in NFSFT and improve parallelization. (#72)
- fastsum: Skip nearfield (pre-)computations when `eps_I` is zero. (#73)
- OpenMP parallelization of NFSOFT. (#81)

### Fixed

- `_Complex` is not supported by some compilers. (#83)

## [3.4.1] - 2018-04-12

### Added

- Compile MEX interface against GNU Octave in TravisCI. (#52)
- Add bash script to build statically linked libs in Windows. (#63)
- Add Octave tests. (#65)
- Add NFSFT Matlab class. (#68)

### Fixed

- Add LaTeX for target `dist` in Travis. (#60)
- `ABS_SRCDIR` might return a wrong path. (#66)
- infft1d is missing in release. (#70)
- Solve compatibility problem with MATLAB 2018a.
- Fix wrong libs flag when compiling for Octave and non-combined fftw3_threads.

## [3.4.0] - 2017-10-21

### Added

- Support cross-compiling (thanks GitHub user xantares). (#30)
- Add API to query window function name. (#35)
- Add Matlab MEX interface for fastsum application. (#39)
- Add Matlab MEX interface for NFCT and NFST modules. (#40)

### Changed

- Change definition of `NFFT_EPSILON` to 2^(1-MANT_DIG) to allow for better
  estimation of error bounds when using long double. (#29)
- Use more efficient method to find log base 2 of an integer. (#58)

### Removed

- Remove defunct iterS2 application. (#54)

### Fixed

- NFSOFT crashes due to false memory free. (#29)
- Support FFTW3 compatible libraries that do not require `-l` linker flags,
  e.g. Intel MKL. (#32)
- Maximum number of plans too low. (#31)
- `nfft_adjoint()` crash with small `N_total`. (#34)
- Build of Octave interface fails in fastsummex. (#50)
- Use MinGW implementation of printf. (#55)
- Internal compiler error with GCC 7 in fastsum. (#57)
- Replace `%td` in format strings with macro `__D__` for Windows
  compatibility. (#59)

## [3.3.2] - 2016-10-16

### Added

- Add support for GNU Octave via MEX interface. (#25)
- Enable query of versioning information. (#27)

### Fixed

- `make check` crashes on Windows. (#20)
- Testsuite failures on selected architectures with 3.3.1. (#24)

## [3.3.1] - 2016-04-24

### Added

- Allow to select scope of unit tests via configure. (#3)

### Changed

- Extend Travis CI configuration. (#1)

### Fixed

- NFFT/NFST/NFCT transforms fail when using certain window functions. (#2)
- NFSFT module crashes due to pointer type incompatibility. (#11)
- `applications/fastsum/fastsum_matlab` produces wrong results in Windows. (#14)
- Fixes for Matlab applications/examples in Windows. (#15)
- `X(bsplines)(n, x)` can be inaccurate when x is close to zero. (#16)
- MATLAB r2015b/r2016a don't ship symlink libmfftw3.so to libmfftw3.so.3. (#17)
- Define format string for `ptrdiff_t` in platform-dependent macro. (#18)

## [3.3.0] - 2016-03-09

### Added

- Add unit tests for some parts of the library. They are invoked via
  `make check`, but only if the CUnit framework was found on the build host.

## 3.2.4

### Fixed

- Fix an issue when linker flags were not set correctly.

## 3.2.3

### Fixed

- Add a workaround for an internal compiler error occurring with gcc 4.7.1
  in kernel/mri.
- Add a workaround for a compilation error in the MATLAB MEX interface for
  gcc 4.7.1 when compiling with C99 support (`-std=gnu99`).

## 3.2.2

### Fixed

- Fix several problems introduced in version 3.2.1.
- Fix an issue when the configure script would not run correctly when using
  the option `--with-fftw3`.

## 3.2.1

### Fixed

- Add missing files of new nfft MATLAB (class) interface to release.

## 3.2.0

### Added

- Add support for OpenMP. To activate, use the configure script with the
  `--enable-openmp` option.
- Add ticks.h from FFTW to leverage CPU cycle counters. If cycle counters
  are available, the configure script will try to determine the number of
  ticks per second. If successful, example programs measure times in seconds.
  Otherwise, example programs will output raw cycle counter differences in
  arbitrary units. If cycle counters are not available, results of time
  measurements are undefined.

### Changed

- Rename functions of direct (non-fast) algorithms to
  `<function name of fast algorithm>_direct`, e.g. the function name for the
  direct computation of the non-equispaced Fourier transform is
  `nfft_trafo_direct(nfft_plan)` instead of `ndft_trafo(nfft_plan)`.

## 3.1.4

### Added

- Add pkg-config file (thanks Gert Wollny).

### Changed

- Headers include/nfft3util.h, applications/fastsum/fastsum.h, and
  applications/fastsum/kernels.h can now be included by C++ compilers.
- All programs from the application and examples subdirectories are no longer
  installed. The same holds for the Matlab code from the matlab subdirectory.

### Fixed

- Fix an error that occurred when trying to create symbolic links to Matlab
  MEX files during installation.

## 3.1.3

### Changed

- Doxygen generated documentation is now only deleted if the target
  maintainer-clean is used. The documentation is no longer deleted if the user
  invokes the usual clean target.

### Fixed

- Fix some issues that can cause C++ compilers to fail. Thanks to Romain Bossart.
- Fix an error that caused linking against FFTW while checking compiler
  characteristics in the configure script. This only affected installations
  where FFTW had been installed in a custom location.

## 3.1.2

### Fixed

- Fix a bug in `fpt_precompute()` that caused excessive stabilization and
  incorrect results.
- Fix three bugs in the nfft: window function defines are moved to the
  internal header infft.h, a larger lookup table is used for `PRE_LIN_PSI`, and
  `nfft_adjoint` for d=2,3 and `PRE_FULL_PSI` writes its output correctly.

## 3.1.1

### Fixed

- Add a workaround for an internal compiler error occurring with gcc 4.3.2.

## 3.1.0

### Added

- A module, called nfsoft, for fast Fourier transforms on the rotation group
  SO(3) has been added.
- It is now possible to configure the build process so that only specific
  modules are compiled and installed. Invoke the configure script with option
  `--help` for details.

### Changed

- The handling of how to link against the fftw3 library has been improved. The
  new configure script options `--with-fftw3`, `--with-fftw-includedir`, and
  `--with-fftw-libdir` allow to specify where fftw3 has been installed.
- Improved compliance with GNU standards.
- The experimental Matlab interface has been improved and is now officially a
  part of NFFT3. To compile the Matlab modules, invoke the configure script
  with the option `--with-matlab=<path/to/matlab/directory>`. Also, an
  interface to the plain NFFT has been added.

### Fixed

- The FPT example program, that is, examples/fpt/simple_test has been
  modified to not require the NFCT module anymore. This solves the problem
  that NFFT won't compile when the FPT module has been switched on while the
  NFCT module is switched off.

## 3.0.2

### Fixed

- Fix a bug in the fpt module that lead to wrong output.

Versions 3.2.4 and older have no GitHub release. Release dates and detailed
release notes are not available for these versions.

